    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1500" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">af-frĕmo</span></b>  (better <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adf-</span></b> ), ĕre, 3, v.
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
			roar</i>, <i>rage</i>, <i>growl</i>, or
				<i>murmur at</i> (only in post-Aug. poets): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adfremit his (Mars),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 528</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Boreas stridentibus adfremit alis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					14, 124</span></i>
			.</div>
